    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn EPD mode, an Encoder request can fail before multimodal input IDs have been generated. For example, `/scheduler_receive_meta_data` may return HTTP 502 when the Encoder connection is reset.\n\nThe Language server then creates an abort request with `origin_input_ids=None`. While streaming the error response, `OutputStreamer` calls `len(req.origin_input_ids)`, raising a `TypeError` and causing the scheduler process to exit. A request-level Encoder failure therefore brings down the Language server.\n\n## Modifications\n\nNormalize missing input IDs to an empty token array when constructing an abort request in the Encoder receiver. This allows the existing abort path to report the Encoder error without crashing the scheduler. Successful requests are unaffected.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model computation or successful-request path is changed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this change only affects error handling.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41646132200](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41646132200)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41646132073](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41646132073)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41646132358](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41646132358)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
